@local/dsh-visual-sandbox README · Install：**Requires** DeepSeek Harness (desktop app or `dsh web`) with a working profile.
The plugin ships as a bundle package — install it from your clone, not from npm.

```bash
git clone https://github.com/Surenkh/dsh-visual-sandbox.git
```

Then register it in `~/.dsh/profiles/<profile>/package.json`:

```jsonc
{
  "dependencies": {
    "@local/dsh-visual-sandbox": "link:../../path/to/dsh-visual-sandbox"
  },

A git dependency works too, if you would rather not keep a local clone:

@local/dsh-visual-sandbox README · Use it：The panel can also be opened from the sparkle mark — the same button closes it again — or by
the agent through `open_visual_sandbox`. Opening always restores the newest preview for the
Session, so the workbench never lands empty.

@local/dsh-visual-sandbox README · Versions：A URL preview, or a file that has no history yet, leaves the field inactive and disabled with
the text **Latest**. Snapshots live in Host memory for the process lifetime, capped at 8
versions / 8 MB per Session; documents larger than 2 MB stay previewable but are not recorded.

@local/dsh-visual-sandbox README · Development：No bundler, no transpiler. Edit `client.js` or `index.js` and reload the Harness page.

```bash
git clone https://github.com/Surenkh/dsh-visual-sandbox.git

@local/dsh-visual-sandbox README · link it into a profile, edit, reload — repeat：```

Ship a change by bumping `version` in `package.json`, adding a `CHANGELOG.md` entry and
tagging the commit.
